      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e host_stage does encode `PKVM_NOPAGE`? it feels like it should e.g. `_pkvm_host_reclaim_page` would call `__host_check_page_state_range(phys, PAGE_SIZE, PKVM_NOPAGE)` and expects to have `host_state \u003d\u003d PKVM_NOPAGE` here.\n\nYep, PKVM_NOPAGE is \u0027cached\u0027 into the vmemmap too, see how host_stage2_set_owner_locked() updates it.\n\n\u003e But it seems we aren\u0027t always updating this flag: e.g. `handle_host_mem_abort-\u003ehost_stage2_idmap` doesn\u0027t seem to flip it.\n\nThat changes an invalid host-owned PTE into a valid one, but that is not an ownership change, so WAI I think :)",
